  "step": [
    {
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1,
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Adding a new bathroom can feel like a big undertaking, and one of the first things people wonder about is permits. It's true, there are often permits and inspections needed, especially when you're adding new plumbing lines, changing the structure, or upgrading ventilation. The time it takes to get these permits can really vary; for building permits, you might wait anywhere from one to eight weeks, and for plumbing, electrical, or HVAC permits, it could be one to four weeks. It really depends on your local jurisdiction here in the Denver area. A common mistake people make is thinking a bathroom addition is just about finishing touches. In reality, it involves a lot of behind-the-walls work like plumbing, electrical, and ventilation coordination. That's why it's so important to get those permits sorted and understand the lead times. You don't want to get halfway through a project only to find out you've missed a crucial step! If your project involves new plumbing lines, structural changes, or significant ventilation upgrades, a licensed contractor who's familiar with the permit process is invaluable. They can help ensure everything is done to code, avoiding costly rework and failed inspections down the road. Don't hesitate to ask for help when dealing with the nitty-gritty of permits and regulations."
    }
  ],
